        "title": "The die is a whole number from 1 to 6",
        "description": "roll is set to a random whole number whose smallest possible value is 1 and largest is 6: a random number with its decimal dropped by floor (or int, Math.floor), and a range or a + 1 that makes it start at 1. Remember the top of random(a, b) is never reached. A round() of a random number from 1 to 6 also stays inside 1 to 6 and counts. Not met: a decimal with nothing dropping the decimal part, a range that can give 0 or 7, or a range that can never give 6. Help: 5.2.2 (Reading: Random numbers and timers)",
