        "title": "A one-shot at frame 300",
        "description": "The code tests frameCount === 300 (or == 300, or against 5 * 60, or against a variable holding 300), which is true on one frame only. A test with >= or > on its own would act on every frame after 300, so it is not met unless something else stops it from repeating. Help: 5.2.2 (Reading: Random numbers and timers)",
